# SRE Dashboard & Observability Demo Bible

This guide is your ultimate cheat sheet for the presentation. It explains the design, query math, and live demonstration steps for each of your panels.

---

## 🏛️ Part 1: The Core Infrastructure

Your application is deployed as a **Decoupled Microservices Architecture** in your OpenShift Namespace (`devops-learning`):
1. **Frontend Tier (`go-frontend-app`)**: Serves the user interface. It has no access to the database for security reasons. It uses JavaScript to pull data from the Backend API.
2. **Backend Tier (`go-backend-app`)**: Connects to the PostgreSQL database, processes user authentication, runs background checks, and exposes Prometheus metrics.
3. **Database Tier (`postgres-db`)**: A PostgreSQL instance backed by a **10 GB PersistentVolumeClaim (`postgres-pvc`)** for data durability.

