## 🧠 Part 3: Q&A Cheat Sheet (Impress your Mentor)

* **Q: Why does PostgreSQL stay around 319 MB even after cleaning it?**
  * *Answer*: PostgreSQL pre-allocates **Write-Ahead Logs (pg_wal)** of 16MB each to guarantee data recovery in case of system crashes. This is normal, healthy database engine overhead.
* **Q: What is the difference between Memory and Storage in your database YAML?**
  * *Answer*: Memory (256MB RAM) is the temporary, high-speed workspace used to run queries. Storage (10GB PVC) is the permanent virtual hard drive volume where the actual database files are saved in the cloud.
* **Q: Why does the Sysdig Agent find your metrics automatically?**
  * *Answer*: Because we annotated our Kubernetes deployment manifest with `prometheus.io/scrape: "true"` and `prometheus.io/port: "8080"`. The Sysdig Agent automatically queries the Kubernetes API for annotated pods, discovers their IPs, and scrapes their `/metrics` pages.
